{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BzCYf7ZerggD8cAhe9PgoL","type":"tool_result","content":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\tb60c8a7d55a78e0c4db474df\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tAditya Kousik (Jira)\ndate:\t2026-03-31T22:40:00Z\nsubject:\t[jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20387) Extend RecordHeader API for Common Value Types\nthread:\tJIRA.13646870.1774996797000@Atlassian.JIRA\nin-reply-to:\tJIRA.13646870.1774996797000@Atlassian.JIRA\n\nAditya Kousik created KAFKA-20387:\n-------------------------------------\n\n             Summary: Extend RecordHeader API for Common Value Types\n                 Key: KAFKA-20387\n                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20387\n             Project: Kafka\n          Issue Type: Improvement\n          Components: clients\n            Reporter: Aditya Kousik\n\n\nRecordHeader values are raw byte[], requiring manual ByteBuffer conversion at every read and write site. We should consider adding static factories (ofString, ofInt..) and typed accessors (stringValue(), intValue() ...) for the common types used in headers. See [KIP-1308|http://example.com]\n\n\n\n--\nThis message was sent by Atlassian Jira\n(v8.20.10#820010)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bdc0be4-9093-40b1-97b8-a699b708e7c0","uuid":"664ec085-3da7-4878-bdf8-707ddd6dbe55","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:44:07.543Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\tb60c8a7d55a78e0c4db474df\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tAditya Kousik (Jira)\ndate:\t2026-03-31T22:40:00Z\nsubject:\t[jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20387) Extend RecordHeader API for Common Value Types\nthread:\tJIRA.13646870.1774996797000@Atlassian.JIRA\nin-reply-to:\tJIRA.13646870.1774996797000@Atlassian.JIRA\n\nAditya Kousik created KAFKA-20387:\n-------------------------------------\n\n             Summary: Extend RecordHeader API for Common Value Types\n                 Key: KAFKA-20387\n                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20387\n             Project: Kafka\n          Issue Type: Improvement\n          Components: clients\n            Reporter: Aditya Kousik\n\n\nRecordHeader values are raw byte[], requiring manual ByteBuffer conversion at every read and write site. We should consider adding static factories (ofString, ofInt..) and typed accessors (stringValue(), intValue() ...) for the common types used in headers. See [KIP-1308|http://example.com]\n\n\n\n--\nThis message was sent by Atlassian Jira\n(v8.20.10#820010)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
